WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.710
(helicopter rotors rumbling)

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.543
- [Shelby] After striking

00:00:02.543 --> 00:00:04.770
a new military base
deal in the Philippines,

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.360
the US is making moves

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.480
to counter China's growing
militarization of the Pacific.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.120
- China's military buildup is astonishing.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.590
To some, it's impressive.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.570
- And it's not showing
any signs of slowing down.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.000
- It's not showing any
signs of slowing down.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.100
- [Shelby] These troops trained
for a potential conflict

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.890
on islands just a hundred
miles from Taiwan,

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.600
the self-ruled island that China

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.479
has threatened to take
by force if necessary.

00:00:27.479 --> 00:00:29.460
(munitions whooshing)

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.080
And powerful American weapons

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.060
were tested over the South China Sea,

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.800
where China's militarized islands

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.360
are threatening its neighbors.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:41.360
- What the US is doing now,
we wish it did decades back.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.080
- [Shelby] But after more than 20 years

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.720
of Chinese expansion,
can the US and its allies

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.840
successfully change the balance
of power in the Pacific?

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.420
(artillery firing)

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.460
The Philippines, a US treaty ally,

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.860
lies southeast of mainland China.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.110
To its west is the South China Sea,

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:01.050
a global shipping route
full of natural resources.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:04.710
And to the north is Taiwan,
a key US trading partner.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.350
Beijing says both Taiwan
and much of the sea

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.410
are part of China, and has
ramped up its military presence

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:11.670
to bolster those claims.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:12.503
- [Reporter] How concerned are you

00:01:12.503 --> 00:01:15.780
with the continued provocation from China?

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.653
- As concerned as you could possibly be.

00:01:18.653 --> 00:01:22.050
It is one of the major
issues that we have to face.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:23.400
- [Shelby] The Philippines' new president,

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.670
Ferdinand Bongbong Marcos
Jr., has leaned into the US

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.190
after years of a more pro-China policy

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.830
under his predecessor, Rodrigo Duterte.

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:34.830
This year, Washington and
Manila struck a major base deal

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.450
that increased the number of sites

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.600
the US can use in the
Philippines from five to nine

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.390
under the Enhanced Defense
Cooperation Agreement.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.670
The new sites bring the US military closer

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.490
to both Taiwan and the South China Sea.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:50.070
And the deal allows the
US to build facilities,

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:53.150
position equipment, and rotate
troops through the bases.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:57.400
(Tan speaking in foreign language)

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.440
- The new sites have angered China,

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.670
which has accused the US

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:05.610
of intentionally stoking
regional tensions.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.350
One of the phrases that I've heard

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.690
is the US could use these bases

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.300
as staging grounds against China.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.590
Is that what they are?

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:16.500
- I think you could
feasibly see that they are,

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.290
but we wouldn't do any of that

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.600
without the consent of
the Philippine Government.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.400
China is a free and sovereign nation.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.420
And as long as they act

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.190
within the international-based,

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:28.470
rules-based order here in the region,

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:31.380
they have plenty of room to operate.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.270
- [Shelby] Major General
Joseph Ryan commands

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:35.640
the Army's 25th Infantry Division.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.240
We met him on the USS Miguel
Keith in the Luzon Strait.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.340
The Luzon Strait is a strategic waterway

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.110
that's a major commercial shipping lane

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.310
and a key transit point

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.250
for both the Chinese and US militaries.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.320
In the event of a conflict over Taiwan,

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.828
control of the strait would be critical.

00:02:51.828 --> 00:02:52.661
(soldier speaking in foreign language)

00:02:52.661 --> 00:02:54.840
- [Shelby] Chinese exercises
in and around the strait

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.630
have heightened concerns
about a war in the region.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.220
And because the US and the Philippines

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.280
have a mutual defense treaty,
the US would be obligated

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.380
to defend the country if it's attacked.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:05.550
- Geography matters.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.460
There's certainly a sense
that should a conflict occur

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:13.020
in Taiwan, that the
Philippines would be affected.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:14.340
- Is the US prepared to fight?

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.540
- Absolutely.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:16.715
And that's what we're doing here.

00:03:16.715 --> 00:03:18.480
(upbeat music)

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.820
- We followed Major General
Ryan and his joint unit

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.470
onto Marine Ospreys and traveled

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:25.023
to some of the northernmost
islands in the Philippines.

00:03:25.023 --> 00:03:27.240
(helicopter rotors whirring)

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.800
The objective of the drill,

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.990
to secure the area and then expand it,

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:34.320
making room for even bigger
firepower like this HIMARS,

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.480
an offensive weapon system that's capable

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.600
of reaching the southern part
of Taiwan from this island.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.150
- A HIMARS rocket system
on the island here

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:45.870
could certainly influence
not only the land space

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.120
but the maritime space

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.580
beyond just where it sits
here on Basco Island.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.470
- [Shelby] Along the coast
of the South China Sea,

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:55.470
the US and Philippine
militaries conducted live fires

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:58.110
of the HIMARS and other
advanced American weapons,

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:01.263
like Stingers and Patriots,

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.960
marking a major escalation of
the exercises from years past.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.960
(soldiers cheering)

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:14.520
For years, Beijing has used
this so-called nine-dash line

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.490
to roughly outline what
it says belongs to China.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.620
The dashes are believed
to be based on maps

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:22.560
used by the Republic of China in 1947.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.020
Within those lines, these satellite images

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:28.140
show how China has turned
reefs into artificial islands

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:30.420
and added airstrips, missile silos,

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:31.890
and communication towers.

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:33.990
- That offends Filipinos.

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:37.830
It's like you always have a
dagger pointed towards you.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.330
- [Shelby] General Emmanuel Bautista

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:41.910
became the chief of staff of
the Philippine Armed Forces

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:45.330
in 2013, the year the
Philippines took China to court

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:47.160
over its contested claims.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.590
The Philippines won the landmark case,

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:52.650
but China has refused
to recognize the ruling.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:55.470
To maintain control, its
ships have repeatedly harassed

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.910
its neighbors' coast guard vessels

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:58.710
and civilian fishing boats,

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.140
blocking their passage with larger ships,

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:04.470
military grade lasers,
and even water cannons.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:08.430
- China is violating our
sovereignty and sovereign rights.

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:10.380
And regardless if there is a competition,

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:12.720
we have an issue with
China in that respect.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.220
- [Shelby] Polls show most Filipinos

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:16.170
support stronger ties with the US

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.360
to help the country
defend its sovereignty.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.710
And despite China's warnings

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:22.020
not to interfere in the South China Sea,

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.670
the country is in talks with the US

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.740
and other Pacific allies like Japan

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:28.050
to launch joint patrols later this year.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:31.170
- Our goal is peace,

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:34.980
security, stability, and
creating opportunity.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:38.010
It's not to engage in a new Cold War,

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:39.510
it's not to contain China.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:41.820
- [Shelby] Some experts
say it might be too late

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.340
to change the balance
of power in the region.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:47.970
China now has more naval
ships, more ICBM launchers,

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:49.440
more active service members,

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:52.110
and potentially more
sophisticated missile capabilities

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:53.190
than the US.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:56.130
But the US is counting on
its alliances in the Pacific

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:57.240
to push back.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:00.240
And in recent months, Washington
has increased security ties

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:03.090
with Japan, Australia, and South Korea.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:06.450
And it has pledged to expedite
weapon sales to Taiwan.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:10.440
- The asymmetric
advantage of our alliances

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:13.560
and partnerships in the region

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:17.490
is part of what separates us from the PRC,

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:18.810
because they don't have that.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:19.650
- The relationships.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.360
- They don't have the relationships.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:26.360
Combat-credible forces,
allied and together,

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:27.480
win wars.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:28.950
So if conflict happens,

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.158
I'm confident we're prepared to fight it.

00:06:31.158 --> 00:06:36.158
(helicopter rotors whirring)
(lighthearted music)

